From: CipherScope <dev@cipherscope.io>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:17:39 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 26/34] test: cover the cross-wallet P2MR multisig PSBT flows

A tmr() leaf is an ordinary BIP342 tapscript, so it can hold a multi_a()
multisig that no single wallet can satisfy. Two wallets, each holding one
private key and the other participant's public key, import the same tree in
two spellings, derive the same bcrt1z address, and co-sign a spend of it
both serially, by passing the serialized PSBT along, and in parallel, by
signing independent copies and merging them with combinepsbt.

A second tree puts the multisig leaf beside a single key leaf that one of
the wallets alone can satisfy, which pins the leaf selection: both leaves
are satisfiable at finalization time and the smaller witness wins.
